(doc
  (title "YBS Step 14 (Swift): SimplePacketBuilder (Test Helpers)")
  (source-format markdown)
  (converted "2026-07-19")
  (para "**Step ID:** `ybs-step_j4k5l6m7n8o9` **Language:** Swift **System:** YX Protocol **Focus:** Test helpers for interoperability testing")
  (section
    (heading "Prerequisites")
    (item "✅ Step 13 completed (Security - Replay Protection + Rate Limiting)")
    (item "✅ Python Step 14 completed (reference implementation)")
    (item "✅ Specifications: `protocol/specs/architecture/api-contracts.sxp`"))
  (section
    (heading "Overview")
    (para "Implement **SimplePacketBuilder** - a synchronous test helper pattern that enables clean interop testing.")
    (para "**Purpose:**")
    (item "Build complete YX packets (HMAC + GUID + payload) without async complexity")
    (item "Support Protocol 0 (Text) and Protocol 1 (Binary) packet building")
    (item "Enable simple sender programs: build → send → exit")
    (item "Match Python API exactly for cross-language testing")
    (para "**Key Insight:** This pattern took SDTS 3-4 days to discover. The problem: Full YX implementation uses actors/async, making simple test senders complex. Solution: Provide synchronous packet-building utilities that don't require event loops or actors.")
    (para "**Pattern:**")
    (code "// Test sender (simple, synchronous)
let packet = try SimplePacketBuilder.buildTextPacket(message, guid: guid, key: key)
try UDPHelper.send(packet: packet, to: \"127.0.0.1\", port: 49999)
exit(0)

// Test receiver (full async implementation)
actor Receiver {
    // Full YX stack with protocol routing, etc.
}"))
  (section
    (heading "What This Step Builds")
    (para "Implements `SimplePacketBuilder` — a Swift facade over `PacketBuilder` reducing boilerplate for common operations in tests and application code."))
  (section
    (heading "Traceability")
    (para "**Specifications:**")
